{
  "_comment": "MODEL L (Assamese) synthetic reasoning lexicon and templates. Consumed by common/reasoning_data.py. Keys beginning with an underscore are documentation.",

  "_review": [
    "The author does not read Assamese fluently, so these templates are",
    "the part of Phase 3 most in need of a native speaker's check. They",
    "were kept deliberately few and structurally simple -- genitive -ৰ,",
    "comparative -তকৈ, question particle নেকি -- so that each one can be",
    "verified in isolation, and every rendered example in the report can",
    "be traced to exactly one line of this file."
  ],

  "_agreement": [
    "Assamese does not mark gender on adjectives, but it does mark",
    "classifiers and honorifics. As in Telugu, comparisons are phrased on",
    "the attribute noun -- 'ৰাজুৰ বয়স গীতাৰ বয়সতকৈ বেছি', Raju's age is",
    "more than Gita's age -- which avoids choosing a classifier per name."
  ],

  "_digits": [
    "ASCII digits. See telugu/configs/reasoning.json: Assamese digits",
    "merge into multi-digit pieces in this tokenizer, which would make",
    "numeric comparison a different task for Model L than for Model H."
  ],

  "prompt_prefix": "প্ৰশ্ন:",
